(with absence of any decent food in the stores being an additional incentive).
- I don't think they actually ate trilobytes though ;-)

   Due to various reasons, I didn't get much of this stuff though;
probably, the most adventurous thing I remember eating were flat sea worms
- about a 20 cm  long, with lots of legs on the sides.  They looked OK
when floating, somewhat...uh...unusual fried, on the plate, but tasted 
pretty good, much like sprats.

   I have a suspicion that there can't be that much adventure in the
world of foods, since our sensory ability in this area is pretty much
limited, and to a great extent has already been experienced -
